  "rationale": "The agent did execute a Comet search against the stated mzML and FASTA, but its delivered TSV is not a valid peptide-spectrum-match report. Its extraction AWK uses the wrong Comet TXT field positions: the captured TXT header puts plain_peptide in column 12 and protein in column 16, while the code exports columns 13 and 17. The execution log demonstrates the consequence: e.g., the first source hit has peptide VPTVPPPR and protein tr|A9EUI2|A9EUI2_SORC5, but the submitted row is VPTVPPPRM and protein 1. Thus peptide sequences have been contaminated with the next flanking residue and protein_accession is instead protein_count. The agent also selected five hits per spectrum under materially different search parameters, whereas the reference runs a high-resolution 5 ppm, 0.03 Da, fully tryptic Trypsin/P, charge 2–4, isotope 0/1 search with one hit and converts idXML accessions. The 2,273 incorrect exported rows versus 375 reference PSMs are therefore not an acceptable implementation difference.",
